{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00302",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.34,
      "end_seconds": 4.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.76,
      "text": "Good morning, how are you doing today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 4.8,
      "end_seconds": 5.61,
      "duration_seconds": 0.81,
      "text": "Hi. Thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 6.46,
      "end_seconds": 9.84,
      "duration_seconds": 3.38,
      "text": "Thank you for fitting us in, um, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 10.3,
      "end_seconds": 14.14,
      "duration_seconds": 3.84,
      "text": "Absolutely, come and sit beside them. How can I help you today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 14.7,
      "end_seconds": 17.72,
      "duration_seconds": 3.02,
      "text": "I've been dealing with a ring-shaped itchy patch."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 18.35,
      "end_seconds": 20.38,
      "duration_seconds": 2.03,
      "text": "How long have you had it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 20.95,
      "end_seconds": 28.4,
      "duration_seconds": 7.45,
      "text": "It's, It's been going on for about two weeks. My family kept telling me to get it checked."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 30.51,
      "end_seconds": 39.47,
      "duration_seconds": 8.96,
      "text": "Alright, tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 40.7,
      "end_seconds": 59.1,
      "duration_seconds": 18.4,
      "text": "It's a couple of times a week. Pretty mild, if I'm being honest. I notice it more with sweating. I'd rather not end up on lots of tablets if I can avoid it. I've also had itching between the toes. So, with itching between the toes, it's all the time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 60.67,
      "end_seconds": 64.27,
      "duration_seconds": 3.6,
      "text": "What about darker skin around the patch, have you noticed that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 65.1,
      "end_seconds": 67.57,
      "duration_seconds": 2.47,
      "text": "Yes, about the same, three weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 68.9,
      "end_seconds": 70.25,
      "duration_seconds": 1.35,
      "text": "Any pain or fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 71.28,
      "end_seconds": 74.05,
      "duration_seconds": 2.77,
      "text": "I haven't had pain or fever, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 75.25,
      "end_seconds": 78.77,
      "duration_seconds": 3.52,
      "text": "Any pus or rash on the palms at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 79.18,
      "end_seconds": 83.69,
      "duration_seconds": 4.51,
      "text": "No, you know, no pus or rash on the palms."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 85.15,
      "end_seconds": 86.51,
      "duration_seconds": 1.36,
      "text": "Do you drink alcohol?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 86.93,
      "end_seconds": 90.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.56,
      "text": "I have a couple of drinks on the weekend."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 92.69,
      "end_seconds": 95.25,
      "duration_seconds": 2.56,
      "text": "What medicines are you taking at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 95.56,
      "end_seconds": 98.6,
      "duration_seconds": 3.04,
      "text": "It's glimepiride, before breakfast for my sugar."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 99.99,
      "end_seconds": 101.84,
      "duration_seconds": 1.85,
      "text": "Do you know the dose?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 102.22,
      "end_seconds": 107.8,
      "duration_seconds": 5.58,
      "text": "2 milligrams. I'm on iron tablets, once a day for my blood count."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 108.68,
      "end_seconds": 110.96,
      "duration_seconds": 2.28,
      "text": "How long have you been on it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 112.07,
      "end_seconds": 116.37,
      "duration_seconds": 4.3,
      "text": "About three months now. I'm on Candid cream, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 117.17,
      "end_seconds": 120.16,
      "duration_seconds": 2.99,
      "text": "Moving on to your background, any past medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 120.82,
      "end_seconds": 138.1,
      "duration_seconds": 17.28,
      "text": "Diabetes, for about a year. I'm not great at remembering details, so bear with me. Low haemoglobin, for nearly five years. Sorry, I know I'm rambling a bit. I wasn't sure whether to come in at all, to be honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 140.89,
      "end_seconds": 156.95,
      "duration_seconds": 16.06,
      "text": "Okay. What I'm doing here is putting together three things: what you tell me, what I find when I examine you, and what the tests show. None of those alone is enough, which is why we sometimes need to wait for results before being certain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 157.65,
      "end_seconds": 159.47,
      "duration_seconds": 1.82,
      "text": "I appreciate you explaining that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 159.79,
      "end_seconds": 161.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.05,
      "text": "Any allergies I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 162.36,
      "end_seconds": 163.12,
      "duration_seconds": 0.76,
      "text": "No allergies."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 165.25,
      "end_seconds": 169.12,
      "duration_seconds": 3.87,
      "text": "Do you need me to explain anything as we go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 169.5,
      "end_seconds": 176.65,
      "duration_seconds": 7.15,
      "text": "I mean, um, just tell me in plain language, please. I'm not good with the medical terms."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 177.13,
      "end_seconds": 179.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.02,
      "text": "Let me check your vitals now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 186.53,
      "end_seconds": 188.01,
      "duration_seconds": 1.48,
      "text": "Hold still for me..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 206.72,
      "end_seconds": 215.73,
      "duration_seconds": 9.01,
      "text": "Okay: pressure 124 over 82, temperature is 36.9 degrees, respiratory rate 18, SpO2 99 percent on room air, pulse is 78 beats a minute."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 218.55,
      "end_seconds": 221.35,
      "duration_seconds": 2.8,
      "text": "Let me have a look at you now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 223.07,
      "end_seconds": 224.77,
      "duration_seconds": 1.7,
      "text": "Take a breath for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 231.95,
      "end_seconds": 237.33,
      "duration_seconds": 5.38,
      "text": "There's a red ring-shaped scaly patch with a clearer centre in the groin crease."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 242.31,
      "end_seconds": 260.26,
      "duration_seconds": 17.95,
      "text": "That's fine, you can get dressed. Thank you for that. I'll write up what I found in a moment, and then I'll tell you what I think is going on. So, based on the history and the examination, it fits best with a fungal skin infection."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 261.76,
      "end_seconds": 266.8,
      "duration_seconds": 5.04,
      "text": "I've been thinking the worst, to be honest. Is it bad?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 267.2,
      "end_seconds": 283.18,
      "duration_seconds": 15.98,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now a fungal skin infection is my leading thought, not anything worse. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had a ring-shaped itchy patch for about two weeks, mild, and no fever or pus."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 283.61,
      "end_seconds": 284.87,
      "duration_seconds": 1.26,
      "text": "That's it, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 286.31,
      "end_seconds": 300.02,
      "duration_seconds": 13.71,
      "text": "I'll be straight with you about how this works. Most of what we see in clinic turns out to be manageable, and the history you give me is often more useful than any single test, so thank you for being so detailed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 301.42,
      "end_seconds": 303.38,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "Thank you, that really helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 304.77,
      "end_seconds": 327.41,
      "duration_seconds": 22.64,
      "text": "Let's get a skin scraping, for suspected fungal infection. The result will help us decide whether anything more is needed. I'm prescribing fluconazole, 150 milligrams, once a week, for two weeks. It's for fungal infection. It's a commonly used medicine and most people tolerate it well. Keep the area dry, wear loose cotton, and don't share towels."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 328.26,
      "end_seconds": 351.31,
      "duration_seconds": 23.05,
      "text": "Try to keep a simple diary of when it happens and what you were doing, and bring it to the next visit. Make sure you're drinking plenty of fluids, two to three litres a day if you can, and get proper rest. Keep an eye out, and if the symptoms get worse, call us the same day or go to emergency."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 352.81,
      "end_seconds": 353.51,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Understood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 353.95,
      "end_seconds": 364.54,
      "duration_seconds": 10.59,
      "text": "I'd like to see you again in two weeks. Just so I know I've explained it clearly, can you tell me the plan back in your own words?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 366.09,
      "end_seconds": 374.19,
      "duration_seconds": 8.1,
      "text": "So, uh, I take the fluconazole, 150 milligrams, once a week and come back in two weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 375.05,
      "end_seconds": 379.44,
      "duration_seconds": 4.39,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. All right, I'll let you go. Any final questions first?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 379.88,
      "end_seconds": 384.81,
      "duration_seconds": 4.93,
      "text": "Yeah, okay, thank you. I'll get started on all of that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 385.7,
      "end_seconds": 387.78,
      "duration_seconds": 2.08,
      "text": "Bye for now, look after yourself."
    }
  ]
}